# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets header rules (docs/INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md §17). Providing this
# file replaces vinext's own auto-generated `_headers` entirely rather than merging with it (see
# §17), so the `/assets/*` immutable rule below is carried forward on purpose — dropping it would
# be a real regression, not a no-op.
#
# Paths not matched by any rule below keep Cloudflare's own platform default (cacheable, but
# revalidated on every use) — correct as-is for the HTML shells and `.rsc` payloads this app emits,
# so they are deliberately not overridden here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- security headers
# Applies to every response this deployment serves. Cumulative with the cache rules below —
# Cloudflare merges all matching rules rather than taking only the first.
#
# ## Why this exists when app/layout.tsx already sets a CSP
#
# The layout ships a `<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">` because GitHub Pages has no
# server to attach response headers with, and `_headers` is a Cloudflare Workers Static Assets
# feature that Pages does not read. So the two deployment targets need two different delivery
# mechanisms for the same policy, and both must exist.
#
# The header is not merely a duplicate: per spec, a `<meta>` CSP cannot enforce `frame-ancestors`
# or `sandbox` at all — they are header-only directives, silently ignored in a meta tag. That made
# clickjacking protection impossible on either target while the meta tag was the only mechanism.
# It is now enforced wherever a real header can be sent, which is the Cloudflare deployment. The
# GitHub Pages export remains unable to express it; that gap is a property of the host, not of
# this policy, and is disclosed in docs/INTEGRATION_GUIDE.md's Known gaps.
#
# The directives below deliberately match app/layout.tsx's meta policy, and
# tests/staticHeaders.test.ts asserts they stay in sync, so a change made in one place cannot
# quietly leave the other target on the old policy.
#
# `'unsafe-inline'` on script-src/style-src is an existing, documented tradeoff, unchanged here:
# the RSC hydration payload ships as an inline `<script>` whose content differs per prerendered
# page, and CustomizationButton's paint swatches use inline `style`. `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` is
# required by the vendored Draco/Basis decoders' Emscripten glue; `connect-src` needs `blob:` and
# `data:` because GLTFLoader's internal loaders fetch both. See app/layout.tsx for the full
# rationale and how each was verified.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' blob: data:; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  # Legacy companion to frame-ancestors, for user agents that predate CSP Level 2.
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Content-hashed build output (vite/vinext's own chunk naming, e.g. BuilderApp-<hash>.js): a new
# build always produces a new hash, so these can be cached forever without a staleness risk.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Everything below is real asset weight that is NOT content-hashed (the file path never changes
# across an edit — scripts/fix-donor-geometry.mjs and scripts/compress-glb.mjs both edit
# public/models/*.glb in place, §1 and §15), so none of it is safe to mark `immutable`. A day's
# cache still meaningfully cuts repeat-visit cost for what includes the single largest asset this
# app ships (the ~1.2 MiB base 4Runner GLB, §15) without risking a stale asset surviving past the
# next deploy for more than a day.
/models/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
/draco/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
/renders/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
/chessathon/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

# The static-export mirror of GET /api/v1/** (scripts/generate-static-api.ts's prebuild output,
# served from here only on the GitHub Pages deployment target where there is no live Worker) —
# matches the Cache-Control the real endpoints send for the same data (app/api/v1/vehicles/**).
/catalog/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# The self-contained Chessathon mini-app (public/chessathon/). Hand-written filenames with no
# content hash — `app-core.js` keeps its path across edits — so it gets the same bounded staleness
# as the other non-hashed asset directories rather than `immutable`.
/chessathon/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate
